---
# Curated for this codebase deliberately, not clang-tidy's defaults:
# - Qt's parent/child ownership model is the correct way to manage memory
#   here, not a bug - cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory/modernize-*'s
#   smart-pointer suggestions would fight the framework, not improve it.
# - readability-*/cppcoreguidelines-* naming/style checks encode a
#   different convention than this project's own (Qt-style camelCase,
#   underscore-prefixed private members) - flagging every symbol as
#   "wrong" isn't useful signal.
# Keeps categories that catch real bugs/perf issues regardless of style:
# bugprone-*, performance-*, clang-analyzer-* (static analysis: leaks,
# null derefs, use-after-free), and a small set of narrowly-scoped
# modernize-*/misc-* checks that are safe, mechanical, and non-stylistic.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  performance-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  modernize-use-override,
  modernize-use-nullptr,
  misc-unused-using-decls,
  misc-unused-alias-decls,

WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '^/home/sharjith/Projects/ModelViewer-Qt/(src|include)/'
FormatStyle: none
